WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:00.600
Our journey

00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:02.836
begins in Pearl Harbor, Hawaii,

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:04.637
the bustling hub of the U.S.

00:00:04.637 --> 00:00:05.872
Pacific fleet,

00:00:05.872 --> 00:00:07.874
covering almost half the world,

00:00:08.141 --> 00:00:10.510
100 million square miles.

00:00:10.877 --> 00:00:14.280
1500 aircraft and around 200 ships,

00:00:14.614 --> 00:00:16.683
including more than half of the Navy's

00:00:16.683 --> 00:00:18.752
nuclear powered submarines.

00:00:19.185 --> 00:00:20.854
Today, we're getting an exclusive

00:00:20.854 --> 00:00:23.189
look inside the USS Mississippi,

00:00:23.490 --> 00:00:23.890
one of the

00:00:23.890 --> 00:00:26.359
most powerful warships on the planet

00:00:27.927 --> 00:00:30.597
with a crew of around 140 people.

00:00:30.930 --> 00:00:32.065
Rear Admiral Jeff

00:00:32.065 --> 00:00:34.334
Javelin is commander of the Pacific Fleet

00:00:34.334 --> 00:00:35.869
Submarine Force.

00:00:35.869 --> 00:00:38.705
Facing new powerful threats in the hotly

00:00:38.705 --> 00:00:40.840
contested Indo-Pacific.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:42.442
Are you concerned about what China's

00:00:42.442 --> 00:00:43.076
Navy is

00:00:43.076 --> 00:00:44.577
doing, particularly in the South China

00:00:44.577 --> 00:00:46.179
Sea and around Taiwan?

00:00:46.179 --> 00:00:47.447
I am concerned.

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:48.948
You know, in today's world,

00:00:48.948 --> 00:00:50.150
we are facing two

00:00:50.150 --> 00:00:51.484
nuclear adversaries

00:00:51.484 --> 00:00:53.553
where we've never had that before.

00:00:53.553 --> 00:00:54.587
The Soviet Union

00:00:54.587 --> 00:00:55.522
and post-Soviet

00:00:55.522 --> 00:00:57.690
in Russia was our peer adversary.

00:00:57.757 --> 00:00:58.458
We're now facing

00:00:58.458 --> 00:00:59.059
China,

00:00:59.059 --> 00:01:00.693
which has expanded and modernized

00:01:00.693 --> 00:01:02.829
their nuclear capabilities.

00:01:02.829 --> 00:01:05.999
The Mississippi is one of 49 fast attack

00:01:05.999 --> 00:01:08.101
submarines in the U.S. naval fleet.

00:01:08.468 --> 00:01:11.504
The fleet also has 14 larger submarines

00:01:11.738 --> 00:01:12.972
carrying nuclear

00:01:12.972 --> 00:01:14.808
armed ballistic missiles.

00:01:14.808 --> 00:01:16.342
The U.S., U.K.

00:01:16.342 --> 00:01:17.310
and Australia's

00:01:17.310 --> 00:01:19.512
newly announced Orcas partnership

00:01:19.512 --> 00:01:20.046
will send

00:01:20.046 --> 00:01:22.715
nuclear powered submarines to Perth,

00:01:23.149 --> 00:01:25.018
potentially challenging China's

00:01:25.018 --> 00:01:26.753
ambitions for the region.

00:01:26.753 --> 00:01:29.656
Beijing now has the world's largest navy,

00:01:29.889 --> 00:01:30.557
but U.S.

00:01:30.557 --> 00:01:31.991
submarines have the world's

00:01:31.991 --> 00:01:33.960
most advanced technology.

00:01:33.960 --> 00:01:36.663
A key advantage in underwater warfare.

00:01:36.963 --> 00:01:38.498
Mississippi is ready to die,

00:01:38.498 --> 00:01:40.800
die, die, die.

00:01:41.401 --> 00:01:43.970
This sub is capable of diving deep

00:01:43.970 --> 00:01:45.105
and fast,

00:01:45.105 --> 00:01:46.706
descending hundreds of feet

00:01:46.706 --> 00:01:47.941
in a matter of seconds,

00:01:47.941 --> 00:01:51.511
300 feet at angles of up to 25 degrees.

00:01:51.811 --> 00:01:53.913
Even standing up can be a challenge

00:01:54.314 --> 00:01:55.048
400 feet,

00:01:55.048 --> 00:01:56.216
traveling underwater

00:01:56.216 --> 00:01:57.250
makes the submarine

00:01:57.250 --> 00:01:59.385
almost impossible to detect.

00:01:59.786 --> 00:02:02.088
The nuclear reactor is so quiet,

00:02:02.388 --> 00:02:04.390
the submarine makes less noise

00:02:04.557 --> 00:02:05.692
than a whale

00:02:05.692 --> 00:02:07.427
in the dark depths of the ocean.

00:02:07.427 --> 00:02:09.462
There's no light to navigate.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.897
Construct 099 on this.

00:02:10.897 --> 00:02:13.766
The team relies on highly sensitive sonar

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:15.335
while the ocean

00:02:15.335 --> 00:02:17.036
environment is very unforgiving.

00:02:17.036 --> 00:02:18.304
So there are a lot of challenges

00:02:18.304 --> 00:02:19.572
that prevent

00:02:19.672 --> 00:02:20.273
a submarine

00:02:20.273 --> 00:02:21.908
from hearing another submarine

00:02:21.908 --> 00:02:23.810
or another surface ship.

00:02:23.810 --> 00:02:25.345
And you've got to be able to understand

00:02:25.345 --> 00:02:26.813
those different challenges.

00:02:26.813 --> 00:02:27.981
The USS Mississippi,

00:02:27.981 --> 00:02:28.815
like all of America's

00:02:28.815 --> 00:02:30.850
nuclear submarines, can't essentially

00:02:31.651 --> 00:02:32.585
sustain itself

00:02:32.585 --> 00:02:34.287
under the water for weeks or even months

00:02:34.287 --> 00:02:36.122
at a time because of the nuclear reactor

00:02:36.122 --> 00:02:37.223
that powers them.

00:02:37.223 --> 00:02:39.392
They breathe recirculated air

00:02:39.592 --> 00:02:40.960
and purified water.

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:41.961
The only thing that they need

00:02:41.961 --> 00:02:43.229
to actually get

00:02:43.229 --> 00:02:44.297
resupplied with

00:02:44.297 --> 00:02:45.965
is food for the crew members.

00:02:45.965 --> 00:02:47.100
And that means that they get used

00:02:47.100 --> 00:02:49.135
to spending a very long time

00:02:49.135 --> 00:02:51.037
not only without sunshine and blue skies,

00:02:51.037 --> 00:02:52.005
but also

00:02:52.005 --> 00:02:53.740
without regular communication

00:02:53.740 --> 00:02:55.909
or conversations with their families.

00:02:55.909 --> 00:02:57.443
The food on submarines

00:02:57.443 --> 00:02:59.379
is surprisingly good,

00:02:59.379 --> 00:03:00.580
but spending months

00:03:00.580 --> 00:03:02.348
underwater can be tough.

00:03:02.348 --> 00:03:04.317
No mobile phones allowed

00:03:04.317 --> 00:03:05.685
outside communication

00:03:05.685 --> 00:03:07.887
only possible on e-mails.

00:03:07.887 --> 00:03:09.889
Sailors have to look after each other.

00:03:10.290 --> 00:03:12.559
What most surprised you about life

00:03:12.559 --> 00:03:14.761
in working on a submarine?

00:03:14.761 --> 00:03:15.395
Honestly,

00:03:15.395 --> 00:03:16.229
what surprised me

00:03:16.229 --> 00:03:17.397
the most was like the people,

00:03:18.865 --> 00:03:20.233
how close you get with each other.

00:03:20.233 --> 00:03:22.335
These kind of the shared hardships

00:03:22.335 --> 00:03:22.969
you share with each other.

00:03:22.969 --> 00:03:24.537
You end up with a really strong bond.

00:03:24.537 --> 00:03:26.639
The crew relies on that bond,

00:03:26.639 --> 00:03:27.407
carrying out

00:03:27.407 --> 00:03:29.509
complicated, dangerous tasks

00:03:29.809 --> 00:03:31.578
inside the torpedo room.

00:03:31.578 --> 00:03:32.378
Trident

00:03:32.612 --> 00:03:33.813
technicians practice

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.982
loading high precision weapons

00:03:35.982 --> 00:03:38.384
capable of taking out other submarines

00:03:38.384 --> 00:03:39.519
and ships

00:03:39.519 --> 00:03:40.353
and warning,

00:03:40.353 --> 00:03:42.055
understanding, warning

00:03:42.055 --> 00:03:43.323
at the back of the sub.

00:03:43.323 --> 00:03:44.624
Jack O'Brien works

00:03:44.624 --> 00:03:46.693
with a team of technical engineers.

00:03:47.193 --> 00:03:48.695
Do you ever get bored on a sub?

00:03:48.695 --> 00:03:50.163
No, no, absolutely not.

00:03:50.163 --> 00:03:51.831
Every day I come in thinking

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:52.765
I know what I'm thinking.

00:03:52.765 --> 00:03:53.733
I know exactly

00:03:53.733 --> 00:03:55.335
what's going to happen, what I got to do.

00:03:55.335 --> 00:03:57.103
Rear Admiral Javelin says

00:03:57.103 --> 00:03:59.172
deterrence is the key objective.

00:03:59.505 --> 00:04:01.174
Even winning a war against

00:04:01.174 --> 00:04:02.575
an increasingly powerful

00:04:02.575 --> 00:04:04.177
China would likely result

00:04:04.177 --> 00:04:07.046
in devastating losses for both sides.

00:04:07.146 --> 00:04:07.914
I'm confident

00:04:07.914 --> 00:04:10.950
that should we be called upon to fight

00:04:11.150 --> 00:04:12.385
and hopefully that will never

00:04:12.385 --> 00:04:14.220
happen, that we would win.

00:04:15.255 --> 00:04:17.657
Submarines like the USS Mississippi

00:04:17.824 --> 00:04:20.059
are constantly preparing for war,

00:04:20.426 --> 00:04:23.263
ready at a moment's notice for whatever

00:04:23.329 --> 00:04:27.233
the future holds.

00:04:27.233 --> 00:04:27.867
And the footage,

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.736
they're well, was incredible.

00:04:29.736 --> 00:04:31.771
And when you think about it,

00:04:31.771 --> 00:04:33.239
you've got that nuclear submarine

00:04:33.239 --> 00:04:34.407
watching for threats from China.

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.541
But China, we now know,

00:04:35.541 --> 00:04:37.710
is home to the biggest Navy in the world.

00:04:37.710 --> 00:04:38.845
So from your reporting,

00:04:38.845 --> 00:04:39.946
having these conversations,

00:04:39.946 --> 00:04:41.581
what would the reality of a conflict

00:04:41.581 --> 00:04:44.851
with China actually look like?

00:04:45.652 --> 00:04:46.853
China does have a big navy,

00:04:46.853 --> 00:04:49.022
but they don't have the number

00:04:49.022 --> 00:04:50.456
of nuclear submarines, nuclear

00:04:50.456 --> 00:04:51.991
powered submarines that the United States

00:04:51.991 --> 00:04:53.726
has, both ballistic missile

00:04:53.726 --> 00:04:55.261
and also these attack subs

00:04:55.261 --> 00:04:57.030
that can essentially travel

00:04:57.030 --> 00:04:58.765
around completely undetected.

00:04:58.765 --> 00:05:00.199
It is virtually impossible

00:05:00.199 --> 00:05:01.267
to know where they are

00:05:01.267 --> 00:05:02.101
and they can track

00:05:02.101 --> 00:05:03.436
other countries, submarines

00:05:03.436 --> 00:05:04.704
that are louder

00:05:04.704 --> 00:05:06.306
because a lot of them are diesel

00:05:06.306 --> 00:05:07.707
and just don't have the same level

00:05:07.707 --> 00:05:09.509
of sophisticated technology.

00:05:09.509 --> 00:05:10.843
So then the weapons that they use,

00:05:10.843 --> 00:05:11.878
they can take out subs,

00:05:11.878 --> 00:05:13.046
they can take out ships,

00:05:13.046 --> 00:05:14.180
they can take out,

00:05:14.180 --> 00:05:15.848
you know, targets on the ground.

00:05:15.848 --> 00:05:16.582
So a lot of war

00:05:16.582 --> 00:05:17.517
game simulations

00:05:17.517 --> 00:05:19.152
say that that China could lose up

00:05:19.152 --> 00:05:21.654
to 70 or 80% of its naval fleet

00:05:21.654 --> 00:05:23.189
if they tried to make it

00:05:23.189 --> 00:05:24.390
to invade Taiwan.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:25.325
However,

00:05:25.325 --> 00:05:26.492
it would result in thousands

00:05:26.492 --> 00:05:27.660
of casualties on both sides.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:28.161
The U.S.

00:05:28.161 --> 00:05:29.595
would also lose significant assets,

00:05:29.595 --> 00:05:31.597
including, you know, aircraft carriers.

00:05:31.597 --> 00:05:32.365
Basically, Erin,

00:05:32.365 --> 00:05:33.433
there would be no winners

00:05:33.433 --> 00:05:34.634
in a war over Taiwan.

00:05:34.634 --> 00:05:35.902
That's the message that the U.S.

00:05:35.902 --> 00:05:38.137
is trying to send. Yeah, awful.

00:05:38.171 --> 00:05:39.038
All right. Thank you very much.

00:05:39.038 --> 00:05:39.605
Will Ripley.

